<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walter de Burgh, 1st Earl of Ulster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1230–1271</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walter de Burgh was an Anglo-Irish lord who held the lordship of Connacht and was created Earl of Ulster by Henry III's son Lord Edward in 1263 or 1264, after the death of Hugh de Lacy. His family became the most powerful in Ireland, and his son Richard, the Red Earl, extended its rule over much of the north and west.</p></div>
